  "question_text": "Top-band lines: 6 wall loops against a 3-wall control on the same plate",
  "hypothesis": "E-027's 6-wall strip showed no ripples, but the owner saw its horizontal face lines more evident than E-026's. The slice shows the outer wall identical; the 6-wall build has no sparse infill from 11.6 to 16.6 mm and its layers run 4-6 s longer. On separate plates this is confounded (witness abnormal, layer time 16.9 s vs 10.3 s).",
  "prediction": "On one plate, with equal layer times, the 6-wall strip shows the same faint or no ripples as the 3-wall strip. If its face lines are still more evident, wall count is a likely cause; if they match, the plate or the witness piece caused the earlier difference.",
  "why_this_test": "Puts both wall counts on one plate with a shared anchor, so the earlier comparison's three confounds drop out.",
